{#- The Brief widget's card (main.ts bodies.brief, renderRounds, renderNaming): the brief read from its file, its sizes
    under their creative and channel, its rounds with an update just pulled (one size new, one going), and the files'
    names left automatic. -#}
{%- from "panel/ui.njk" import hot %}
{%- set a = panel.art %}
<div class="pt-card ag">
  <div class="ag-sec">
    {%- call hot(1) %}
    <div class="ag-head"><span class="ag-label">Brief</span><span class="ag-meta">{{ a.brief.file }} · {{ a.brief.sheet }} · {{ a.brief.sizes }} sizes</span></div>
    <div class="ag-btns"><span class="ag-btn ag-import">{{ a.importIcon | safe }}Open brief…</span></div>
    {%- endcall %}
    {%- call hot(2) %}
    <div class="ag-chips">
      {%- for g in a.brief.groups %}
      {%- for s in g.sizes %}
      {%- set chip %}<span class="ag-chip is-on{% if s.diff %} is-{{ s.diff }}{% endif %}">{{ s.label }}</span>{% endset %}
      {%- if loop.first %}<span class="ag-group"><span class="ag-ch">{{ g.label }}</span>{{ chip | safe }}</span>{% else %}{{ chip | safe }}{% endif %}
      {%- endfor %}
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
    {%- endcall %}
    <p class="ag-meta">Read from line {{ a.brief.header }}'s headers: {{ a.brief.columns }}. Each row is a size in a channel, for a creative; a print row's size is its trim in mm after its scale.</p>
    {%- call hot(3, true) %}<span class="ag-btn ag-sm">Type the sizes instead</span>{% endcall %}
  </div>
  <div class="ag-sec">
    <div class="ag-head"><span class="ag-label">Rounds</span><span class="ag-meta">round {{ a.rounds.now }} of {{ a.brief.file }}</span></div>
    {%- call hot(4, true) %}
    <span class="ag-rounds">{% for n in a.rounds.list %}<span class="ag-round{% if n == a.rounds.now %} is-now{% endif %}">{{ n }}</span>{% endfor %}</span>
    {%- endcall %}
    {%- call hot(5) %}<p class="ag-meta">The update: 1 new, 1 going. New and going sizes are orange on the nodes, going ones struck through; a changed size's card says what changed. Apply keeps round {{ a.rounds.now }}'s files in Superseded/v{{ a.rounds.now }}, the going sizes' moved out of the output.</p>{% endcall %}
    {%- call hot(6, true) %}<span class="ag-btns"><span class="ag-btn ag-sm ag-primary">Apply updates</span><span class="ag-btn ag-sm">Discard</span></span>{% endcall %}
    {%- call hot(7) %}<div class="ag-row"><span class="ag-meta ag-grow ag-ellipsis">Kept in {{ a.rounds.kept }}</span><span class="ag-btn ag-sm">Show in Finder</span></div>{% endcall %}
  </div>
  <div class="ag-sec">
    <div class="ag-head"><span class="ag-label">File names</span></div>
    {%- call hot(8) %}
    <div class="ag-row"><span class="ag-meta ag-job">Job number</span><span class="ag-input ag-grow is-empty">123456</span></div>
    <p class="ag-meta">Automatic: each file is named by its size, as “[Masters] 1080x1920.idml”; a size in two channels is one file. A job number names them by tags.</p>
    <div class="ag-btns"><span class="ag-btn ag-sm">Name them by tags</span></div>
    {%- endcall %}
  </div>
</div>
